    CandidateGenerator <|.. GridGenerator
    CandidateGenerator <|.. RandomGenerator
    CandidateGenerator <|.. DomainGuidedGenerator
    CandidateGenerator <|.. GeneticGenerator
    GridGenerator <.. RandomGenerator : builds bounded pool
    GridGenerator <.. DomainGuidedGenerator : filters
    GridGenerator <.. GeneticGenerator : seeds pool

    Store --> DiscoveryFunctions : proposes one candidate
    Store --> DiscoveryValidationFunctions : freezes split and assesses
    DiscoveryFunctions --> SelectionFunctions : selects generator/parents
    DiscoveryFunctions --> DiscoveryProposalValidator : validates LLM candidate
    DiscoveryFunctions --> DiscoveryLLMHTTPAdapter : optional typed provider
    Store --> DiscoveryCandidateExperiments : persists phase links
    Store --> DiscoveryAssessment : archives terminal outcome
    Store --> DiscoveryTrialReservation : tracks four-job budget
    EventWorker --> Store : advances after evaluation commit
    Store --> CandidateEnvelope

    note for CandidateGenerator "services/search.py uses this duck-typed shape.<br/>domain/search/contract.py remains a separate richer Protocol and is not consumed by current generators."
    note for CandidateEnvelope "Conceptual name for the persisted candidate dict.<br/>No CandidateEnvelope dataclass exists in the current runtime."
    note for DiscoveryFunctions "No DiscoveryController class exists. Mutation, crossover and ensemble are function branches over archive parents; LLM is DiscoveryLLMHTTPAdapter callback."
    note for Store "Current durable controller: Store methods own DB transaction and one active candidate.<br/>Admission creates train first; validation jobs follow a passing train."
    note for DiscoveryTrialReservation "Reservation row records reserved_jobs=4; it does not enqueue four jobs upfront.<br/>Test partition is created only after an accepted survivor and normal stop."
    note for DiscoveryCandidateExperiments "Unique candidate/partition/ordinal makes event redelivery and restart reconciliation idempotent."
